rlm-yubikey-ssh-add [-q]

Load the YubiKey PIV keys (e.g. slot 9a, PIV AUTH) into the running
ssh-agent via the PKCS#11 module, prompting for the PIN once. After
that, ssh connections that use the key through the agent do not ask
for the PIN again until the YubiKey is unplugged or the agent restarts.

If no YubiKey is plugged in (Yubico USB vendor id 0x1050 in ioreg)
it returns 0 without prompting; -q suppresses the notice, for use in
shell startup files. If the agent can already sign with
~/.ssh/yubikey-9a.pub it does nothing and skips the PIN prompt.
Otherwise any previous registration of the module is removed first, so
it is safe to run again after replugging the key. The loaded keys are
listed at the end.

Uses /usr/local/lib/libykcs11.dylib because the macOS ssh-agent refuses
PKCS#11 providers outside /usr/lib and /usr/local/lib (symlinks are
resolved first). Copy the Homebrew library there once, and again after
upgrading yubico-piv-tool:

  sudo mkdir -p /usr/local/lib
  sudo cp "$(realpath /opt/homebrew/lib/libykcs11.dylib)" \
    /usr/local/lib/libykcs11.dylib

For ssh to use the agent key instead of prompting on its own, the host
entry should use IdentityFile <key>.pub with IdentitiesOnly yes and no
PKCS11Provider line.

REQUIRES
  ssh-add, yubico-piv-tool (libykcs11.dylib)